{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Lipsync onto an existing video (InfiniteTalk, masked face inpaint + paste-back)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes + VideoHelperSuite + SAM 3.1 + cj_h3_tools. VHS_LoadVideo (25 fps, long edge capped) -> ImageScale to the 480p InfiniteTalk size (plain stretch) -> padded with the last frame so every 81-frame window exists -> SAM 3.1 text track (node 42, default 'face') -> GrowMask -> CJMaskTemporal (max). Each InfiniteTalk pass (Wan 2.1 I2V 480p + lightx2v, 6 steps, CFG 1, single-speaker patch, wav2vec2 on the DRIVING audio) samples from VAEEncode(that window's source frames) with SetLatentNoiseMask(face mask), so outside the face the latent stays the source and inside it the mouth/jaw are generated from noise (the source lips never leak in; only the driving audio moves them). The builder (src/lib/oj/videoLipsync.ts) chains extra passes (previous_frames, 9 motion frames, +72 new frames each, source window [72k, 72k+81)), trims to min(video, audio), CJImagePasteBack keeps the full-res source outside the mask (fit stretch, blob mode off), and CreateVideo muxes the trimmed driving audio (the source audio is dropped). Paste-back tone: region_match 1.0 fits a per-channel mean/std transfer on the face mask's inner rim (the regenerated face drifts a few levels from the source) and grow 14 / feather 10 put the seam ramp outside the regenerated area, where the round-tripped source matches."
  },
